{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem (finding P0-2a — separate from the seam-conversion work)\nprojects_store.set_project (projects_store.py) accepts ANY string key with no validation:\nit does not call fetcher._validate_project_key, so a syntactically-invalid or malformed\nkey (e.g. \"le-g\", \"\", \"1x\", a key with trailing whitespace) is written to projects.json\nand only fails much later, deep in the reconciler fan-out. A validation guard at write\ntime would have rejected the malformed input that contributed to the incident class\n(05b8-4efe-8d58-4c27).\n\n## Scope note\nThis is a NEW behavior (input validation), NOT a hand-rolled->seam conversion. Filed\nseparately from ticket fea4 (pure seam conversion, now merged) so it can be approved on\nits own. It does NOT modify any shared seam and adds no facade. SYNTACTIC validation ONLY —\nNO live Jira/network call (existence validation is owned by the reconcile preflight, not\nhere).\n\n## Approach\nset_project validates the key with the EXISTING fetcher._validate_project_key (import and\nreuse it — do NOT duplicate the _PROJECT_KEY_RE regex `^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*$`) and\nrejects an invalid key with a clear error and NO file write, BEFORE the record is\npersisted/published. remove_project gets the same guard for symmetry (it can receive an\nunvalidated key). The validation slots in BEFORE B's fsutil.atomic_write + write_lock +\ncommit_and_push_tickets_branch RMW, so a rejected key never locks/commits/pushes. No\nJira-existence checking here.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] set_project with an invalid key (\"le-g\", \"\", \"1x\", \"LEG \" trailing space) raises a\n      clear error and writes NOTHING (projects.json unchanged / uncreated), verified by\n      `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_projects_store_heldout.py -q`.\n- [x] A valid key (\"REB\", \"PROJ_2\") is still accepted and written unchanged (B's\n      atomic_write/lock/publish path preserved), verified by the same test module.\n- [x] remove_project rejects an invalid key with the same guard, before any mutation.\n- [x] Reuses fetcher._validate_project_key; no duplicated regex, no seam change, no\n      network/Jira call added.\n\n## Testing\n- RED-first unit tests in tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_projects_store_heldout.py: each\n  invalid key raises and leaves projects.json unwritten; a valid key still writes. Run\n  `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/ tests/scripts/bridge/ -q`.\n- `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean.\n\n## Sequencing\nEdits projects_store.py (+ _lib_ops.py if needed) + tests — same file as ticket fea4, now\nMERGED into origin/main, so this builds on B's seams. This change stacks on B."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786824011114003001,"uuid":"d3eeb07f-7ad1-441c-8afc-a4d39bbcffef"}